s is just going to be  terrible that's the reality the debate  is going to be on Tuesday October 15th  at 8:00 p.m. Eastern Time  we will attempt live coverage of course  and the reality is that no one can look  good with 12 people on the stage  especially when you're answering poorly  framed  chins from the moderators so who's  responsible here is it CNN in the New  York Times for wanting it to be on one  night is it the Democratic National  Committee for accepting that it all be  done on one night who has the power here  it's not completely clear but what I can  tell you for sure what is very clear is  that they are making the debates not  only unwatchable but completely useless  in terms of actually providing us with  the information that we need to  accurately and in an informed way  determine who it is we want to support  in the 2020 Democratic primary it now  let's do a little math if with 12  candidates on stage if the debate ran  three hours with no commercials that's a  hundred and eighty minutes 12 candidates  that's 15 minutes per candidate so  that's already not great look if I'm  going to decide who I'm supporting I  want to hear from them for more than  just 15 minutes but again that's with no  breaks with no anything else remember  that the last CNN debate started with  some overly produced sports game like  introduction opening statements from  candidates which I find completely  useless and a commercial break before  the first question it was 25 minutes  into the scheduled start of the debate  before the first question was asked they  also were scheduled for three hours or  maybe for two but in any case they ended  up twenty minutes shy of three hours so  you take away 25 minutes from the front  you take away 20 minutes from the end  and on that basis each candidate gets a  little over 11 minutes to speak and then  if we add in the fact that they are  taking a couple commercial breaks  throughout the entire thing what you end  up with with 12 candidates on the stage  effectively in a quote three-hour debate  is 10 minutes of speaking time per  candidate this is not how I want to pick  a presidential candidate it's  embarrassingly bad and then of course  there's also the issue of the fact that  with absolutely no chance of winning you  have candidates participating and taking  away from important conversations that  we could be having I'll give you an  example imagine if Bernie Sanders and  Elizabeth Warren and Joe Biden  could spend 45 minutes just the three of  them talking about exactly how their  healthcare plans would work we would be  able to actually press Joe Biden on how  not progressive his health care plan is  Bernie Sanders would be able to actually  hash out with Elizabeth Warren  okay well Elizabeth if you're open to  Medicare for all but you're also open to  other options give me one of those other  options let's debate in detail how one  of the other options would work but it's  not going to happen we're going to hear  from you no irrelevant nonsense from Tom  Styer and Tulsi Gabbard and Amy  Klobuchar and other people who have no  shot at this it's going to be terrible I  will be watching of course but it is not  going to be a debate that will leave us  drastically more informed in depth about  the positions of the candidates that  actually have a shot of this thing  mistakes all around and unfortunately  the debates seem to be getting worse as  we go not better
 

